== Notes ==
* {{dlc+|a+nr}} Suture can be killed by {{i|Little Horn}}.{{dlc-}}
* If encountered in a Double Trouble boss fight, Suture's {{i|Brimstone}} laser can damage the other boss.

== Trivia ==
* Blighted Ovum was added in the ''Wrath of the Lamb'' DLC for the original ''The Binding of Isaac''.
* In the original game, Blighted Ovum could also be encountered in the {{s|Catacombs}}.
* They are the posthumous version of [[Gemini]].
* In medicine, a blighted ovum is a pregnancy in which the early pregnancy appears normal on an ultrasound scan, but later no visible embryo develops.
* {{dlc|nr}} Contusion has skin on his body in the boss art, but he doesn't in-game.
* Blighted Ovum is the only boss in [[chapter 1]] that is a posthumous version of another boss.
** Gemini also shows up in [[chapter 1]], which makes it one of only four bosses to have its posthumous version in the same chapter, the other cases being {{e|Polycephalus}} and {{e|Chub}} having {{e|The Stain}} and {{e|Carrion Queen}}, respectively, in [[chapter 2]]; {{dlc+|r}} and the {{e|Tuff Twins}} having {{e|The Shell}} in [[Chapters|Chapter 2.5]].{{dlc-}}
* In ''Wrath of The Lamb'', when Blighted Ovum was killed, Contusion would shoot 8 extremely fast tears in the cardinal and ordinal directions, and after a short delay, would be followed up by Suture, who would explode similarly.
* In the [[Bestiary]], Suture is referred to as "The Blighted Ovum Baby".
* {{dlc+|r}} Blighted Ovum, {{e|Big Horn}}, {{e|Triachnid}}, {{e|Isaac}}, and {{e|???}} are the only bosses whose portraits were completely changed in ''Repentance'' (beyond simply adding more detail). Of these, only Triachnid, Isaac, and ??? didn't receive new sprites.{{dlc-}}
* In Rebirth, the older boss portrait had Suture smiling in it, which was the 2nd time he had a smile.

